Caminandes 1: "Llama Drama" -- the bundled animation
----------------------------------------------------
`assets/anim/llama/` is the animation `granim` plays (`run granim llama`).
It is a conversion of the Blender Foundation open movie
**Caminandes 1: "Llama Drama"** (2013):

  Title:    Caminandes 1: Llama Drama
  Creator:  Pablo Vazquez
  Producer: Blender Foundation / CineLibre
  Source:   https://archive.org/details/Caminandes1LlamaDrama
  Licence:  Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 (CC-BY 3.0)
            https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/

The excerpt is 15 seconds -- t = 44-59 s of the 90-second film -- cropped to
4:3, desaturated, tone-curved and converted to 360 multicolour `.pic` frames,
then packed as `.anm` chunks by `tools/gen-anim.py`. What is redistributed here
is that converted frame data and nothing else: 60 chunk files and a manifest, in
which no frame is the original picture at its own resolution. It is a **derived
work**, so it carries the same CC-BY 3.0 terms as the film, and this attribution
is what those terms require. The download the frames were extracted from is not
in this repository.

ALF -- the boot banner and the two sample pictures
--------------------------------------------------
